      "title": "Riot police deployed to Poland’s constitutional court after judge suspended",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/31/riot-police-deployed-to-polands-constitutional-court-after-judge-suspended",
      "description": "<p>President Karol Nawrocki seen struggling to gain entry to court building in Warsaw amid long-running row over the court’s legitimacy</p><p>Riot police were locked in a tense standoff with protesters outside Poland’s constitutional court on Friday night after its top judge was suspended in the latest escalation in a decade-long dispute over the court’s legal status.</p><p>The clashes followed a controversial decision by a group of government-appointed judges to suspend the court’s contested president, Bogdan Święczkowski, and his deputy, Bartłomiej Sochański, amid disagreements over the bench’s legitimacy.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/31/riot-police-deployed-to-polands-constitutional-court-after-judge-suspended\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-31T04:27:25"
    },
    {
      "title": "Poland Deploys Riot Police in Standoff Over Country’s Top Court",
      "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/31/world/europe/poland-court-police-president.html",
      "description": "After years of legal wrangling, judges backed by the current government suspended the chief justice, as a feud escalated with the right-wing party that last held power.",
      "source_name": "NYT World News",
      "published": "2026-10-31T15:36:52"
